have excellent writing ability as well, so that the email you send and the
help files you write are clear and concise.

You must be an expert in using a unix system for Internet and Usenet functions.
This does _not_ mean that must be a C programmer (though that wouldn't hurt).
It means that you must be very familiar with all of the standard Unix tools
that Panix users are likely to use and the ability to learn and master new
software packages quickly. You must be able to read and create small shell
scripts in order to accomplish basic maintenance functions. You must have a
strong grasp of basic Telecomm issues (using PCs/Macs and modems).

If you prove to be exceptionally good at this job, there is extraordinary
potential for job improvement here; we'll be hiring more staff in the next
12 months and we will need a senior support person. In addition, you will
have the opportunity to learn a great deal about systems administration;
if you learn enough you may become qualified for the position of System
Administrator, either at Panix or anywhere else.

Your job responsibilities will include:

User Support

*	You must answer questions directed to Panix staff either by email or
by news posting. (We discourage phone calls for technical support, but you
will also answer such calls.)

*	You will identify questions that are asked frequently and extend our
online help system to cover these issues.

*	You will identify additional software and/or services that are
requested by Panix users so that we can consider adding them.

*	You will call people who want to sign up as new users, validate them,
and add them to the system.

Systems Administration

*	You will keep an eye on the system and correct any problems that you
can, or else refer them to other staff members.

*	You will watch over our telephone and T1 lines, either correcting
trouble or referring it to other staff.

*	You will maintain a strict backup schedule, changing tapes as needed
(using software we provide).

*	You will perform and track system changes, creating such paper and
electronic trails as are necessary.

